sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> a prov:SoftwareAgent;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "delphisci dataset-resolvability assessor (Grok 4.7)";
    prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/usesModel> <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7-high-fast>.
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7-high-fast> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LanguageModel>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7";
    dc:identifier "grok-4.7-high-fast".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2023-agential-12--grok> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7 on levin-2023-agential-12: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.55";
    dc:description "The memory operationalization is the right kind: a persistent change in regenerative outcome after a transient stimulus, with a reset. Published planarian experiments report that pattern for wild-type stocks. Those counts are not a reusable dataset, and several non-bioelectric stores fit the same persistence, so existing reports test the phenomenon only in part.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: Treat memory as a regenerative head number that stays altered after a brief physiological treatment is washed out, in animals whose genotype is the wild-type stock, and that can be reset by a later physiological treatment. Stable two-headed regeneration after a two-day treatment, reversible without a genetic change, would support multiple stored targets; immediate reversion after washout, or a mutation that co-segregates with head number, would refute it.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Head-number counts are in the experimental papers, not in a public individual-level file, and the lines have not been shown by a deposited genome to be free of mutations.", "Persistent drug, epigenetic marks, or microbiome changes can store the phenotype without a bioelectric target representation.";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasConfidence> "0.66"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasScore> "0.548"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasVerdict> "partially-resolvable".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2023-agential-12--grok--analysis-feasibility> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Analysis feasibility of levin-2023-agential-12 by Grok 4.7: 0.5";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0-analysis-feasibility>;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0/analysis-feasibility";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasScore> "0.5"^^xsd:double;
    dc:isPartOf <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2023-agential-12--grok>.
